;; flint.deps's own workspace, separate from the stdlib's flint/flint
;; (`DECISIONS.md#flint-deps-is-its-own-workspace`).
;;
;; ITS OWN SOURCE ROOT, `lib/deps/`, so it is owned by CONTAINMENT like every
;; other root: `flint.deps` is `lib/deps/flint/deps.cljc` and its three
;; siblings sit under `lib/deps/flint/deps/`. It used to be governed by the
;; namespace PREFIX "flint/deps" inside `lib/`, which every door had to apply
;; by hand (`DECISIONS.md#four-units`).
;;
;; `.cljc`, NOT `.fln`, ON PURPOSE: the JVM Clojure driver (`bin/flint`) loads
;; `flint.deps`, `flint.deps.manifest` and `flint.deps.registry` as Clojure,
;; and Clojure cannot load a `.fln` (`bin/check` asserts it).
;;
;; Shipped with the native and npm CLIs, and an OPTIONAL building block in the
;; ESM SDK (`@3sln/flint/deps`); never part of the standard library.
;;
;; NO GRANT. `flint.deps`/`flint.deps.manifest`/`flint.deps.registry` are pure
;; data manipulation (`clojure.edn`/`clojure.string` over `deps.edn`,
;; `package.json`, `pom.xml`, a registry document) -- no `:host`-guarded
;; builtin, no virtual namespace require. `flint.deps.resolve` requires the
;; virtual `flint.deps.npm`/`-git`/`-mvn`, but reaching a virtual namespace is
;; gated by a RUNTIME `:with` grant the host checks when the port is opened
;; (`doc/api-review.md`'s "Served, not linked" section), not by this
;; compile-time workspace mechanism.
{:flint/workspace flint/deps}
